  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.95:\n\t\t- Fixed: a report with a resource or instance property filter set failed the whole list of\n\t\t  reports with \"Error reading string. Unexpected token: StartObject\", because\n\t\t  PropertyFilterMetric (added in 3.240.90) typed both filters as strings. LogicMonitor sends\n\t\t  each as null or an object. The new PropertyFilter, PropertyFilterRule and\n\t\t  PropertyFilterExpression model the object, from a live portal's response.\n\t\t- Fixed: ResourceInventoryReport.Metrics was never populated, because it had no DataMember.\n\t\t  ResourceInventoryReportMetric now models what LogicMonitor sends: dataSourceId,\n\t\t  dataSourceFullName and instances. Breaking for anyone who referenced them: its ItemType\n\t\t  and ItemValue properties are removed. They never held data.\n\t\t- ResourceMetricTrendsReport and InterfaceBandwidthReport gain topN.\n\t\t- Every report on two live portals, 376 in all, now reads with both the Release and the\n\t\t  strict Debug settings.",
